cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these skills in your work, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "shuji: skills for coding agents"
abstract: >-
  Portable skills for coding agents in the Agent Skills format: bento-diagrams draws engineering diagrams in Apple's
  system look as one draw.io file for both themes, checked for overlaps; sumi-diagrams writes Mermaid diagrams and
  charts rendered by Pele as one themeable SVG, checked for syntax, overlaps and size, and diagrams of a change for
  pull requests; toryo-loop runs a coding-agent delivery loop as a master session, from a queue of GitHub issues
  through executor subagents in worktrees and a fresh reviewer on another model to pull requests landed and checked.
authors:
  - given-names: Gabriele
    family-names: Durante
repository-code: "https://github.com/exdsgift/shuji-skills"
url: "https://github.com/exdsgift/shuji-skills"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - agent skills
  - coding agents
  - Claude Code
  - Codex
  - diagrams
  - draw.io
  - Mermaid
  - Pele
  - pull requests
  - subagents
  - code review
  - GitHub Issues
